@lang en

-- us-ch2-international-agreements.l4 : Title 1, sections 112a(b) and 112b (international agreements and qualifying
-- non-binding instruments; transparency provisions).
-- Source: usc01.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text); quotation lines copy it.
--
-- Three kinds of function are here. (1) Deadlines: every "N days after" or "N years after" goes through the helper in
-- us-interpretation-time.l4 Part B, which reads "after" in its ordinary sense, because Title 1 has no counting rule
-- (fork F-after). (2) Definitions and exemptions: "means" definitions are exhaustive; "includes" definitions are
-- scoped, so FALSE reads "this clause does not say so". (3) Duties: a duty is encoded as the fact that the section
-- imposes it on the facts given, never as a prediction that it will be met.
--
-- The text uses "month" in "once each month" and "the prior month" (section 112b(a)(1)) and never defines it; those
-- are named refusals at the end of subsection (a). The texts of "the date of the enactment of this section" in
-- subsection (h) and "the date of the enactment of the James M. Inhofe National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal
-- Year 2023" in subsection (l)(2) name an event and no date; the first is an input, the second is a fact the
-- caller supplies (open questions in NOTES.md).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `us-nouns`
IMPORT `us-interpretation-time`

§ `Section 112a(b) and section 112b - international agreements and non-binding instruments`

§§ `Section 112b(b)(3) - what is exempt from posting`

-- The five categories are one record, `An instrument under section 112b`, with one field per limb. Categories (A) to (D)
-- exempt the instrument and also exempt "information described in subparagraphs (A)(iii) and (B)(iii) of subsection
-- (a)(1) relating to" it; category (E) exempts the instrument but keeps that information in, "except that the
-- Secretary shall make the information ... available ... within the timeframes required by paragraph (1) or (2)".
-- src:141 | The requirements under paragraphs (1) and (2) shall not apply to the following categories of international agreements or qualifying non-binding instruments, or to information described in subparagraphs (A)(iii) and (B)(iii) of subsection (a)(1) relating to such agreements or qualifying non-binding instruments:
-- src:142 | (A) International agreements and qualifying non-binding instruments that contain information that has been given a national security classification pursuant to Executive Order 13526 (50 U.S.C. 3161 note; relating to classified national security information) or any predecessor or successor order, or that contain any information that is otherwise exempt from public disclosure pursuant to United States law.
-- src:143 | (B) International agreements and qualifying non-binding instruments that address military operations, military exercises, acquisition and cross servicing, logistics support, military personnel exchange or education programs, or the provision of health care to military personnel on a reciprocal basis.
-- src:144 | (C) International agreements and qualifying non-binding instruments that establish the terms of grant or other similar assistance, including in-kind assistance, financed with foreign assistance funds pursuant to the Foreign Assistance Act of 1961 (22 U.S.C. 2151 et seq.) or the Food for Peace Act (7 U.S.C. 1691 et seq.).
-- src:145 | (D) International agreements and qualifying non-binding instruments, such as project annexes and other similar instruments, for which the principal function is to establish technical details for the implementation of a specific project undertaken pursuant to another agreement or qualifying non-binding instrument that has been published in accordance with paragraph (1) or (2).
-- src:146 | (E) International agreements and qualifying non-binding instruments that have been separately published by a depositary or other similar administrative body, except that the Secretary shall make the information described in subparagraphs (A)(iii) and (B)(iii) of subsection (a)(1), relating to such agreements or qualifying non-binding instruments, available to the public on the website of the Department of State within the timeframes required by paragraph (1) or (2).
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(b)(3)(A) to (E) (src:141 src:142 src:143 src:144 src:145 src:146)
GIVEN instrument IS A `An instrument under section 112b`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112b(b)(3) exempts the text of the instrument from the posting requirements` instrument MEANS
       instrument's `it contains information given a national security classification or otherwise exempt from public disclosure`
    OR instrument's `it addresses military operations, military exercises, acquisition and cross servicing, logistics support, military personnel exchange or education programs, or reciprocal health care to military personnel`
    OR instrument's `it establishes the terms of grant or similar assistance financed with foreign assistance funds under the Foreign Assistance Act of 1961 or the Food for Peace Act`
    OR instrument's `its principal function is to establish technical details for a specific project under another instrument already published under section 112b`
    OR instrument's `it has been separately published by a depositary or other similar administrative body`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(b)(3)(A) to (E) (src:141 src:142 src:143 src:144 src:145 src:146)
GIVEN instrument IS A `An instrument under section 112b`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112b(b)(3) exempts the information on legal authority and implementation from the posting requirements` instrument MEANS
       instrument's `it contains information given a national security classification or otherwise exempt from public disclosure`
    OR instrument's `it addresses military operations, military exercises, acquisition and cross servicing, logistics support, military personnel exchange or education programs, or reciprocal health care to military personnel`
    OR instrument's `it establishes the terms of grant or similar assistance financed with foreign assistance funds under the Foreign Assistance Act of 1961 or the Food for Peace Act`
    OR instrument's `its principal function is to establish technical details for a specific project under another instrument already published under section 112b`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(b)(3)(A) (src:142)
GIVEN instrument IS A `An instrument under section 112b`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument is described in section 112b(b)(3)(A)` instrument MEANS
    instrument's `it contains information given a national security classification or otherwise exempt from public disclosure`

§§ `Section 112a(b) - copies on request`

-- "other than the agreements described in section 112b(b)(3)(A)": category (A) describes both international agreements
-- and qualifying non-binding instruments, and the exclusion is read to take out the whole category (fork F-112a-b).
-- src:123 | (b) Copies of international agreements and qualifying non-binding instruments in the possession of the Department of State, but not published, other than the agreements described in section 112b(b)(3)(A), shall be made available by the Department of State upon request.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112a(b) (src:123)
GIVEN instrument IS A `An instrument under section 112b`
      `it is an international agreement or a qualifying non-binding instrument in the possession of the Department of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a request has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112a(b) requires the Department of State to make the copy available` instrument `it is an international agreement or a qualifying non-binding instrument in the possession of the Department of State` `it has been published` `a request has been made` MEANS
        `it is an international agreement or a qualifying non-binding instrument in the possession of the Department of State`
    AND NOT `it has been published`
    AND NOT `the instrument is described in section 112b(b)(3)(A)` instrument
    AND `a request has been made`

§§ `Section 112b(a) - reports to Congress`

-- INERT, section 112b(a)(1)(A) and (B)(i) and (iii): the lists, the texts and the descriptions of legal authority that the Secretary
-- "shall provide in writing" to the leaders and committees named. The recipients are named bodies and the contents are documents; no
-- fact a downstream encoding asks about turns on them, and every period in them runs on "the prior month", which is refused below.

-- src:128 | Not less frequently than once each month, the Secretary shall provide in writing to the Majority Leader of the Senate, the Minority Leader of the Senate, the Speaker of the House of Representatives, the Minority Leader of the House of Representatives, and the appropriate congressional committees the following:
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(a)(1) (src:128): "once each month" and "the prior month" use a time word Title 1 never defines
GIVETH A DATE
`Title 1 does not say what a month is, so section 112b(a) cannot fix the days of once each month or of the prior month` MEANS
    REFUSE "Title 1 does not say what a month is, so section 112b(a) cannot fix the days of once each month or of the prior month"

