`section 112b(g) allows the agreement to be signed or otherwise concluded on behalf of the United States` `prior consultation with the Secretary has occurred, whether on this agreement or on a class of agreements that includes it` MEANS
    `prior consultation with the Secretary has occurred, whether on this agreement or on a class of agreements that includes it`

§§ `Section 112b(h) - audits by the Comptroller General`

-- "the date of the enactment of this section" names an event. Title 1 prints a date for the section's addition and for its
-- amendments in the source credit, which is not a provision of the text, and does not say which one the words mean (open
-- question O-h in NOTES.md). The date is therefore an INPUT.
-- src:162 | Not later than 3 years after the date of the enactment of this section, and not less frequently than once every 3 years thereafter during the 9-year period beginning on the date of the enactment of this section, the Comptroller General of the United States shall conduct an audit of the compliance of the Secretary with the requirements of this section.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(h)(1) (src:162)
GIVEN `the date of the enactment of this section` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest day for the first audit under section 112b(h)(1)` `the date of the enactment of this section` MEANS
    `the day that is a number of years after a date` 3 `the date of the enactment of this section`

-- "not less frequently than once every 3 years thereafter during the 9-year period beginning on the date of the enactment":
-- a later audit falls due three years after the one before, and is required only if that day is in the nine-year period.
-- The period begins on the enactment day and ends the day before the ninth anniversary (fork F-nine), so with an audit
-- on the third anniversary the next falls due on the sixth, which is in the period, and with an audit on the sixth anniversary
-- the next would fall on the ninth, which is the first day AFTER the period: no further audit is required.
-- src:162 | and not less frequently than once every 3 years thereafter during the 9-year period beginning on the date of the enactment of this section, the Comptroller General of the United States shall conduct an audit of the compliance of the Secretary with the requirements of this section.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(h)(1) (src:162)
GIVEN `the day of the previous audit` IS A DATE
      `the date of the enactment of this section` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest day for the next audit after an audit under section 112b(h)(1)` `the day of the previous audit` `the date of the enactment of this section` MEANS
    `the day that is a number of years after a date` 3 `the day of the previous audit`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(h)(1) (src:162)
GIVEN `the day of the previous audit` IS A DATE
      `the date of the enactment of this section` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112b(h)(1) requires a further audit after an audit` `the day of the previous audit` `the date of the enactment of this section` MEANS
    `a date falls in the period of a number of years beginning on a day`
        (`the latest day for the next audit after an audit under section 112b(h)(1)` `the day of the previous audit` `the date of the enactment of this section`)
        `the date of the enactment of this section`
        9

-- INERT, section 112b(h)(2) to (4): what the Comptroller General does when a failure was due to another agency's failure, the
-- written results he sends, and the publication of them. Duties of an office whose performance no later rule reads.

§§ `Sections 112b(i) and 112b(j)`

-- INERT, section 112b(i): "The President shall, through the Secretary, promulgate such rules and regulations as may be necessary".
-- A duty to make subordinate legislation, with no test and no period.
-- INERT, section 112b(j): "It is the sense of Congress that ...". By its own words a statement of opinion, imposing nothing.

§§ `Section 112b(k) - definitions`

-- (1), (2), (3) and (6) name offices and bodies ("appropriate congressional committees", "appropriate department or agency",
-- "intelligence community", "Secretary") and are INERT: they say who is meant, and a program asks nothing of them.
-- (4) and (7)(A) say "includes", so each is a scoped function: TRUE is "the clause says so", FALSE is "the clause does not say so".
-- src:177 | The term “international agreement” includes—
-- src:178 | (A) any treaty that requires the advice and consent of the Senate, pursuant to article II of the Constitution of the United States; and
-- src:179 | (B) any other international agreement to which the United States is a party and that is not subject to the advice and consent of the Senate.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(k)(4) (src:177 src:178 src:179)
GIVEN `it is a treaty that requires the advice and consent of the Senate under article II of the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an international agreement to which the United States is a party and is not subject to the advice and consent of the Senate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112b(k)(4) expressly includes the matter in the term international agreement` `it is a treaty that requires the advice and consent of the Senate under article II of the Constitution` `it is an international agreement to which the United States is a party and is not subject to the advice and consent of the Senate` MEANS
       `it is a treaty that requires the advice and consent of the Senate under article II of the Constitution`
    OR `it is an international agreement to which the United States is a party and is not subject to the advice and consent of the Senate`

-- (5) says "means": an exhaustive definition. (A) means a non-binding instrument that meets (i) and one of (I) and (II), and
-- (B) takes out one that is signed, becomes operative or is implemented under the authorities relied upon by the Department of
-- Defense, the Armed Forces or an element of the intelligence community.
-- src:180 | The term “qualifying non-binding instrument”—
-- src:181 | (A) except as provided in subparagraph (B), means a non-binding instrument that—
-- src:182 | (i) is or will be under negotiation, is signed or otherwise becomes operative, or is implemented with one or more foreign governments, international organizations, or foreign entities, including non-state actors; and
-- src:183 | (ii)
-- src:184 | (I) could reasonably be expected to have a significant impact on the foreign policy of the United States; or
-- src:185 | (II) is the subject of a written communication from the Chair or Ranking Member of either of the appropriate congressional committees to the Secretary; and
-- src:186 | (B) does not include any non-binding instrument that is signed or otherwise becomes operative or is implemented pursuant to the authorities relied upon by the Department of Defense, the Armed Forces of the United States, or any element of the intelligence community.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(k)(5) (src:180 src:181 src:182 src:183 src:184 src:185 src:186)
GIVEN instrument IS A `A non-binding instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument is a qualifying non-binding instrument` instrument MEANS
        instrument's `it is or will be under negotiation, is signed or becomes operative, or is implemented with foreign governments, international organizations or foreign entities, including non-state actors`
    AND (   instrument's `it could reasonably be expected to have a significant impact on the foreign policy of the United States`
         OR instrument's `it is the subject of a written communication from the Chair or Ranking Member of either appropriate congressional committee to the Secretary`)
    AND NOT instrument's `it is signed, becomes operative or is implemented under the authorities relied upon by the Department of Defense, the Armed Forces or an element of the intelligence community`

-- (7): the "text" of an agreement or instrument includes an annex, appendix, codicil, side agreement, side letter or similar
-- document, and an implementing agreement or arrangement or similar document, "entered into contemporaneously and in conjunction
-- with" it. (B) says that phrase is "construed liberally" and "may not be interpreted to require any action to have occurred
-- simultaneously or on the same day". So no date is an input: whether the two were done on the same day cannot decide the matter,
-- and the input below is the judgment, made liberally, that the document was entered into in conjunction with the instrument.
-- src:189 | The term “text” with respect to an international agreement or qualifying non-binding instrument includes—
-- src:190 | (i) any annex, appendix, codicil, side agreement, side letter, or any document of similar purpose or function to the aforementioned, regardless of the title of the document, that is entered into contemporaneously and in conjunction with the international agreement or qualifying non-binding instrument; and
-- src:191 | (ii) any implementing agreement or arrangement, or any document of similar purpose or function to the aforementioned regardless of the title of the document, that is entered into contemporaneously and in conjunction with the international agreement or qualifying non-binding instrument.
-- src:192 | (B) As used in subparagraph (A), the term “contemporaneously and in conjunction with”—
-- src:193 | (i) shall be construed liberally; and
-- src:194 | (ii) may not be interpreted to require any action to have occurred simultaneously or on the same day.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(k)(7) (src:189 src:190 src:191 src:192 src:193 src:194)
GIVEN `it is an annex, appendix, codicil, side agreement, side letter, or a document of similar purpose or function, regardless of its title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an implementing agreement or arrangement, or a document of similar purpose or function, regardless of its title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was entered into contemporaneously and in conjunction with the agreement or instrument, the phrase being construed liberally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112b(k)(7) expressly includes the document in the text of the agreement or instrument` `it is an annex, appendix, codicil, side agreement, side letter, or a document of similar purpose or function, regardless of its title` `it is an implementing agreement or arrangement, or a document of similar purpose or function, regardless of its title` `it was entered into contemporaneously and in conjunction with the agreement or instrument, the phrase being construed liberally` MEANS
        (   `it is an annex, appendix, codicil, side agreement, side letter, or a document of similar purpose or function, regardless of its title`
         OR `it is an implementing agreement or arrangement, or a document of similar purpose or function, regardless of its title`)
    AND `it was entered into contemporaneously and in conjunction with the agreement or instrument, the phrase being construed liberally`

§§ `Section 112b(l) - rules of non-construction`

-- src:196 | to authorize the withholding from disclosure to the public of any record if such disclosure is required by law; or
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(l)(1) (src:196)
GIVEN `disclosure of the record is required by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112b does not authorize withholding the record from the public` `disclosure of the record is required by law` MEANS
    `disclosure of the record is required by law`

-- (l)(2) names an event, the enactment of the James M. Inhofe National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023, and no date.
-- The caller states the fact that matters: whether the material "was not required to be provided" to the leaders and committees
-- "prior to the date of the enactment" of that Act.
-- src:197 | to require the provision of any implementing agreement or arrangement, or any document of similar purpose or function regardless of its title, which was entered into by the Department of Defense, the Armed Forces of the United States, or any element of the intelligence community or any implementing material originating with the aforementioned agencies, if such implementing agreement, arrangement, document, or material was not required to be provided to the Majority Leader of the Senate, the Minority Leader of the Senate, the Speaker of the House of Representatives, the Minority Leader of the House of Representatives, or the appropriate congressional committees prior to the date of the enactment of the James M. Inhofe National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112b(l)(2) (src:197)
GIVEN `it was entered into by the Department of Defense, the Armed Forces of the United States or an element of the intelligence community, or originated with one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was required to be provided to the leaders and committees before the enactment of the Act of Fiscal Year 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112b does not require the provision of the implementing material` `it was entered into by the Department of Defense, the Armed Forces of the United States or an element of the intelligence community, or originated with one of them` `it was required to be provided to the leaders and committees before the enactment of the Act of Fiscal Year 2023` MEANS
        `it was entered into by the Department of Defense, the Armed Forces of the United States or an element of the intelligence community, or originated with one of them`
    AND NOT `it was required to be provided to the leaders and committees before the enactment of the Act of Fiscal Year 2023`
